{
 "_comment": [
  "Placement oracle for the bridge-2 port. Every unit lands in the EXISTING scratchy crate",
  "`deeptools` under src/bridges/dataflow_ir_to_sentient/ \u2014 one .rs per original dcc translation",
  "unit (conventions.md: one .rs home per C translation unit), grouped into the five modules the",
  "campaign's own crates.json named.",
  "",
  "UNIT NAMES are `e<NNN>_<cppName>` where NNN is the entry number in",
  "crustify-bridge2/source/bridge2.cpp and in crates/compiler/deeptools/docs/bridge2-porting-order.md.",
  "The 268 rewritten member definitions carry that exact symbol in the extract; the remaining 116",
  "in-class definitions keep their bare C++ name there, so ALWAYS resolve a unit through",
  "crustify-bridge2/UNITS.tsv, which gives its entry number, level, authority citation and the",
  "extract's own line range.",
  "",
  "`tu` is the extract for every entry because the extract is the campaign's declared impl_file;",
  "`headers` names the ORIGINAL dcc file(s) the .rs homes, so `crates locate --file dcc/src/...`",
  "resolves. There is no -sys surface: deeptools-sys is an empty placeholder (see its Cargo.toml).",
  "",
  "The bridge-4 module `progir_to_senprog` is UNIONED IN below. The bridge-4 campaign directory's",
  "own crates.json holds ONLY that module, so writing it here verbatim DELETED bridge 2's five",
  "(947 lines) and left `crates locate` unable to resolve any bridge-2 unit while its review",
  "sub-campaign is still running. Both maps live in this one file."
 ],
